Acknowledgments
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Eleven Edit was written independently, from scratch. No third-party source
code is included, copied, or reused.

The Eleven Rack USB / MIDI (SysEx) protocol used by this software was
re-derived independently through direct packet analysis (Wireshark). No Avid
software, firmware, or source code was used at any point.

The SysEx protocol map builds on -- and gratefully acknowledges -- the earlier
reverse-engineering work of:

    Guillaume Schmid -- ElevenHack (2013)
    https://sites.google.com/site/elevenhack/
    ElevenHack is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

ElevenHack was consulted as conceptual reference only. None of its code was
copied, ported, or incorporated; the two projects share no source and are
built on different technology stacks.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
macOS build (Eleven Edit for Mac)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The macOS port, released as "11 Edit" (native CoreMIDI bridge, Mac build,
the Studio interface, the bundled audio driver build), was built by
Damilola Olalere (MrDees) on top of Charles Wardick's Windows editor,
Eleven Edit. "11 Edit" names this Mac build only; the project it is built
from remains Eleven Edit. Charles Wardick wrote the original editor; Guillaume Schmid's
ElevenHack informed the protocol; both remain credited as requested.

The macOS DMG bundles the Eleven Rack audio driver for Apple Silicon:

    Matt Housley -- Eleven Rack Driver (2026), MIT License
    https://github.com/Matt-Housley/eleven-rack-driver

vendored under driver/ (see driver/LICENSE and driver/README-ELEVEN-EDIT.md)
with Eleven Edit's playback fixes on top (driver/History.txt, 1.2.0).

The Mac build bundles two typefaces under the SIL Open Font License 1.1
(src/fonts/, licence texts alongside):

    Manrope -- Copyright 2018 The Manrope Project Authors (Mikhail Sharanda)
    JetBrains Mono -- Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors

Amp, cabinet and effect names shown as "based on" in the interface are
trademarks of their respective owners, who are not associated with this
project or with Avid; they identify the gear whose tones the Eleven Rack
models are based on. Eleven Rack is a trademark of Avid Technology.

